OL,3,CDrought status declared for all of
OL,4,CWales as July set to be driest ever
OL,6,FNatural Resources Wales has announced
OL,7,Fthat drought status has been extended
OL,8,Facross all of Wales as conditions
OL,9,F"continue to deteriorate".
OL,11,FDrought was first declared in north
OL,12,FWales and Upper Severn on 23 July, but
OL,13,Fthe status is now covering the entire
OL,14,Fcountry.
OL,16,FIt comes after Wales has faced
OL,17,Fsuccessive heatwaves, widespread
OL,18,Fwildfires and record-low river levels.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G1/4
