OL,3,CDrought status declared for all of
OL,4,CWales as July set to be driest ever
OL,6,FNatural Resources Wales reported that
OL,7,Fupdated figures show Wales has
OL,8,Freceived just 8% of its long-term
OL,9,Faverage rainfall for July, with this
OL,10,Fmonth on course to be the driest July
OL,11,Fin Wales since records began 190 years
OL,12,Fago.
OL,14,FThe majority of rivers across Wales
OL,15,Fare exceptionally low, including the
OL,16,FRivers Clwyd, Dyfi, Alyn, Clywedog,
OL,17,FDyfi, Conwy, Cleddau, Cothi, Teifi,
OL,18,FWye and Usk.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G2/4
